  "caveats": [
    "Pure-Python baseline uses random.Random(seed).gauss (Mersenne Twister 32-bit plus pair caching), so its stream differs from the C++ engine; the comparison is about cost per path, not bit equality of prices.",
    "Single-threaded on both sides: no OpenMP/TBB in the C++ core, no multiprocessing in the baseline. A multi-core claim would need a different measurement.",
